>Fainting is pretty annoying when you're trying to stay alive.

  None of those patches signal fainting.  Luckily there is an option to
have NetHack make an audible sound of your choice when you start
fainting.  (Not available on NAO.)

  Use the SOUND options in your NetHack options file.  (defaults.nh on
MS Windows).  The following lines should work on MS Windows 98SE.


SOUNDDIR=c:\windows\media 

SOUND=MESG "*feel hungry*"           "Notify.wav" 50
SOUND=MESG "*feel weak*"             "Ding.wav"   50
SOUND=MESG "*You faint*"             "Ding.wav"   50
SOUND=MESG "*You fall asleep*"       "Ding.wav"   50
SOUND=MESG "*You pass out*"          "Ding.wav"   50

>
>Also, how to add daggers to auto-pickup?  (now that I've bent to the
>inescapable need to play wizard as a sideshow knifethrower instead of
>a thaumaturgist, sigh...)   

  An early wizard isn't good enough to be a side show magician.  It's
only after the quest that a wizard starts being a fearsome spellcaster.
(An XL:30 Wizard casting magic missile, finger of death, cone of cold,
and fireball is awesome.)


>I play tiles and don't even know what the icon for dagger is.

  The icon doesn't matter.  Add this line to your options file:

AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTION="<*dagger*"


  You'll also want to use the 'f'ire command in conjunction with
autoquiver.  Turn on autoquiver by adding the following line to your
options file.:


options=AUTOQUIVER


  


